  "facts": [
    "The Richmond–San Rafael Bridge opened September 1, 1956, ending a 41‑year ferry era that began in 1915 and ran until the night of August 31, 1956, when the last ferry crossed the bay.",
    "The bridge’s double‑deck cantilevers rise and dip in a roller‑coaster profile, a cost‑saving design that critics say violates the aesthetic rule that a bridge should soar, earning Frank Lloyd Wright a harsh rebuke.",
    "A seismic retrofit completed in September 2005 cost $778 million, reinforcing the bridge to survive a 7.4‑magnitude Hayward Fault quake, while a full replacement would skyrocket to $16–22 billion."
